      "description": "The paper dialog frame with feedback kept visibly inside the active modal.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\" aria-labelledby=\"ds-dialog-title\"><header class=\"ds-panel-header\"><h2 id=\"ds-dialog-title\">Your saved dives</h2><button class=\"ds-panel-close\" aria-label=\"Close dialog\">×</button></header><div class=\"ds-modal-notice\" role=\"status\">Storage is full or unavailable. This dive could not be saved. Keep it open, free local storage, then try saving again.</div><div class=\"ds-panel-body\"><p>Saved on this device.</p></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:AtollSans,Arial,sans-serif;background:var(--paper,#f4f0df);color:var(--ink,#163c43);width:min(930px,90%);max-height:100%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;box-shadow:0 12px 50px #082b3880;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}.ds-panel-header{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:20px 27px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#c6d0c5);gap:16px}.ds-panel-header h2{margin:0;font-family:AtollDisplay,Georgia,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:29px;line-height:1.2}.ds-panel-close{font-family:AtollSans,Arial,sans-serif;background:none;border:none;font-size:24px;line-height:24px;color:var(--ink,#163c43);padding:7px}.ds-panel-body{padding:23px 27px;overflow:auto;min-height:0}.ds-panel-body p{margin:0;line-height:1.6}.ds-modal-notice{padding:10px 27px;background:#eadbaf;color:#3d4a37;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;flex-shrink:0}.ds-panel-close{transition:background .16s,color .16s;cursor:pointer}.ds-panel-close:hover{filter:brightness(1.06)}.ds-panel-close:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-panel-close:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #f4c76e;outline-offset:3px}.ds-panel-close:disabled{cursor:default;opacity:.48}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-panel-close{transition:none}}@media(max-width:1100px){.ds-panel-header{padding:14px 22px}.ds-panel-header h2{font-size:25px}.ds-panel-body{padding:16px 22px;overscroll-behavior:contain}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sequence Chips",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "sequence-tag",
      "description": "Static species labels for a multistage dive; the first label has a stronger tint.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-sequence\"><span>Neon damselfish</span><span>Parrotfish</span><span>Coral grouper</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-sequence{font-family:AtollSans,Arial,sans-serif;color:var(--ink,#163c43);display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:15px}.ds-sequence span{font-size:10px;background:#dce7d7;padding:5px 8px}.ds-sequence span:first-child{background:#c5dbcb}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Survival Meters and Habitat Map",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Two slim numeric meters and a nine-cell map, extracted from the survival bar.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-instruments\"><div class=\"ds-meters\"><div class=\"ds-meter-row\"><span>Energy</span><div class=\"ds-meter\" role=\"meter\" aria-label=\"Energy\" aria-valuemin=\"0\" aria-valuemax=\"100\" aria-valuenow=\"100\"><i></i></div><span>100</span></div><div class=\"ds-meter-row\"><span>Health</span><div class=\"ds-meter\" role=\"meter\" aria-label=\"Health\" aria-valuemin=\"0\" aria-valuemax=\"100\" aria-valuenow=\"100\"><i></i></div><span>100</span></div></div><div class=\"ds-map\" aria-label=\"Reef section 5 of 9\"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class=\"ds-map-active\"></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-instruments{font-family:AtollSans,Arial,sans-serif;color:var(--ink,#163c43);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:22px;padding:9px 2%;background:#f4f0e0f5;border-top:1px solid #d9d5bd}.ds-meters{display:grid;gap:7px;min-width:175px;flex:1;max-width:290px}.ds-meter-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:47px 1fr 30px;gap:8px;align-items:center;font-size:10px}.ds-meter{height:9px;background:#d1d9cd;border:1px solid #b4c2b8}.ds-meter i{display:block;height:100%;background:#6e9b66;transition:background .18s linear}.ds-meter i.ds-warning{background:#c7a34b}.ds-meter i.ds-danger{background:#c36850}.ds-map{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,13px);grid-template-rows:repeat(3,11px);gap:3px;padding:4px}.ds-map span{border:1px solid #809e94;background:#d7dfcd}.ds-map span.ds-map-active{background:#256a6e}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-meter i{transition:none}}@media(max-width:1100px){.ds-instruments{gap:12px}.ds-meters{min-width:150px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The illustrated living reef",
    "overview": "Richly textured natural-history reef illustrations and crisp side-profile fish carry the experience. Jewel-tone coral, luminous turquoise water, cream sand, and deep cave shadows give the world its detail. Compact warm cream and gray-green controls, dark teal lettering, and Spectral headings provide the field-guide frame.\n\nThe reef dominates this desktop 16:9 scene-driven game. Menus and educational dialogs sit over the same illustrated world; interface density stays compact so the habitat and creatures remain visible. Original artwork, typography, and branding preserve the approved visual direction without copying game marks.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Rich natural-history illustration with clear side-profile creatures.",
      "Nine distinct habitat compositions with scene-specific shelter and food placement.",
      "Warm paper surfaces, restrained teal actions, and compact ecological instruments.",
      "Spectral headings paired with readable DM Sans controls.",
      "Full reef readability in both daytime and nighttime play."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Reef Color Rule",
        "body": "Let the paintings carry the broad color range; keep the interface grounded in paper, ink, and teal.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Distinct Habitat Rule",
        "body": "Each of the nine scenes must have a distinct overall silhouette, negative-space arrangement, and habitat topology. Do not repeat an open-water bowl framed by coral across the map.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Night Rule",
        "body": "Keep nighttime habitats as readable as daytime. The renderer deliberately applies no dark night filter or obscuring fog.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** let original reef paintings and side-profile creatures dominate the stage.",
      "**Do** preserve nine distinct scene silhouettes, negative spaces, and habitat topologies.",
      "**Do** place shelters and food against each painting's actual terrain.",
      "**Do** use Spectral for titles and DM Sans for controls and facts.",
      "**Do** keep energy and health compact, labeled, and numerically readable.",
      "**Do** preserve visible keyboard focus, modal focus containment, and in-dialog feedback.",
      "**Do** keep the night reef fully readable and honor reduced-motion preferences."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** reuse the rejected open-water bowl composition for every habitat.",
      "**Don't** copy original game marks, lettering, or bundled artwork.",
      "**Don't** cover the reef with combat HUD clutter, broad fog, or a dark night filter.",
      "**Don't** replace the compact rectangular controls with oversized pill or card treatments.",
      "**Don't** allow portrait canvases to overflow their stages or obscure text.",
      "**Don't** hide save or load feedback behind the active dialog."
    ]
  }
}
